#
# The scenes a golden image is taken of.
#
#   name | binary | size | arguments…
#
# Pipe-delimited rather than the cases.json the plan called for, and the reason
# is a dependency rather than a preference: parsing JSON from a shell script
# needs jq or python, and D8 in docs/03-tech-stack.md is emphatic that a
# distribution packager should be able to build and check this repository from
# what their distribution already ships. Four fields and no quoting rules is
# also a format a reviewer can read in a diff, which matters more here than
# structure — this file is edited by people deciding what is worth watching.
#
# Blank lines and # comments are ignored. `binary` is `app` or `gallery`.
#
# ---- what is worth a golden ------------------------------------------------
#
# Named scenes, not a sweep. Every case below is either a layout that a change
# elsewhere could plausibly break, or a piece of the design system that has been
# got wrong before. The gallery pages carry their component's name, so a diff on
# `moon.png` says which card moved without anybody opening the image.
#
# Both schemes for the scenes where the two differ structurally — the light
# theme has no stars, a hairline card edge and an inverted accent — and dark
# only for the rest, because a second copy of a page that differs by six
# colours is a second image to re-record for no extra information.

# ---- the desktop page -------------------------------------------------------
desktop|app|1340x762|--scheme dark
desktop-light|app|1340x762|--scheme light
desktop-scrolled|app|1340x900|--scheme dark --scroll 900
desktop-scrolled-light|app|1340x900|--scheme light --scroll 900
desktop-uv|app|1340x762|--scheme dark --metric uv
desktop-uv-light|app|1340x762|--scheme light --metric uv
desktop-list|app|1340x762|--scheme dark --list
desktop-night|app|1340x762|--scheme dark --sky night

# ---- the phone --------------------------------------------------------------
# Every tab, because MobileShell destroys and rebuilds a page on each change and
# four of the five are reachable no other way in a capture.
mobile-today|app|390x844|--scheme dark --viewport mobile
mobile-today-light|app|390x844|--scheme light --viewport mobile
mobile-hourly|app|390x844|--scheme dark --viewport mobile --tab hourly
mobile-monthly|app|390x844|--scheme dark --viewport mobile --tab monthly
mobile-maps|app|390x844|--scheme dark --viewport mobile --tab maps
mobile-me|app|390x844|--scheme dark --viewport mobile --tab me
mobile-me-light|app|390x844|--scheme light --viewport mobile --tab me
mobile-night|app|390x844|--scheme dark --viewport mobile --sky night

# ---- the tablet -------------------------------------------------------------
tablet|app|834x1112|--scheme dark --viewport tablet
tablet-light|app|834x1112|--scheme light --viewport tablet

# ---- severe weather ---------------------------------------------------------
#
# The `seattle` fixture, which is the only one that carries alerts: four of them
# at one coordinate on the afternoon of 5 August 2026, recorded from
# api.weather.gov. Every other case above uses `toronto`, whose alerts.json is
# an empty collection — so a change to the banner cannot silently move any of
# the thirty-two images that came before these.
#
# It has to be a fixture. Alerts are the most volatile product in the app; a
# golden image of a live one would have a shelf life measured in hours.
alert-desktop|app|1340x762|--scheme dark --fixture seattle
alert-desktop-light|app|1340x762|--scheme light --fixture seattle
alert-mobile|app|390x844|--scheme dark --viewport mobile --fixture seattle
alert-mobile-light|app|390x844|--scheme light --viewport mobile --fixture seattle

# All five CAP grades side by side, plus the three states that are about the app
# rather than the weather. This is the image that catches a severity colour
# drifting, and it is the only place four of the five grades appear at all.
gallery-alerts|gallery|1400x1250|--scheme dark Banner
gallery-alerts-light|gallery|1400x1250|--scheme light Banner
gallery-severity-glyph|gallery|900x300|--scheme dark "Severity glyph"

# ---- the design system, as the gallery draws it -----------------------------
# The palette page is the audit instrument; a change to any colour token shows
# up here as a diff on one row, which is the most legible failure in the set.
gallery-colour|gallery|1500x2200|--scheme dark Colour
gallery-colour-light|gallery|1500x2200|--scheme light Colour
gallery-ramps|gallery|1500x1120|--scheme dark Ramps
gallery-ramps-light|gallery|1500x1120|--scheme light Ramps
gallery-type|gallery|1100x900|--scheme dark Type

# ---- individual cards -------------------------------------------------------
# The eight that carry a bespoke visualisation. These are the ones where a
# change to chartmath.js or to a ramp shows up as a shape moving rather than as
# a colour changing, and a per-card image is what names which.
card-temperature|gallery|1100x760|--scheme dark Temperature
card-feels-like|gallery|1100x760|--scheme dark "Feels like"
card-precipitation|gallery|1100x760|--scheme dark Precipitation
card-wind|gallery|1100x760|--scheme dark Wind
card-uv|gallery|1100x760|--scheme dark UV
card-pressure|gallery|1100x760|--scheme dark Pressure
card-sun|gallery|1100x760|--scheme dark Sun
card-moon|gallery|1100x760|--scheme dark Moon
card-moon-light|gallery|1100x760|--scheme light Moon
